From: Ken Zhu <guigenz@codeaurora.org>
Date: Fri, 23 Jul 2021 09:32:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] qca-nss-clients: fix out of memory issue

rtable is not release if it was not set skb_dst

Backport of commit ec7a57bed8914adcbd5bf95de1f0b630296489c1 from the
NHSS.QSDK.11.4 branch of https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-clients
(the 11.4 source c4049d1 used here comes from caf_migration/11.4.0.5.r3,
which does not have it).

nss_tunipip6_encap_exception() looks up an IPv4 route for every exception
packet; when the route does not point to the tunnel, the packet is passed
to netif_receive_skb() without ip_rt_put(), leaking one dst reference per
packet.  On a DS-Lite gateway the leaked dsts can never be freed once the
route cache entry is replaced, so ip_dst_cache (SUnreclaim) grows without
bound.

Change-Id: I6be6332f7b71a7c7a55d6082f055bd6828076be1
Signed-off-by: Ken Zhu <guigenz@codeaurora.org>
---
 tunipip6/nss_connmgr_tunipip6.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/tunipip6/nss_connmgr_tunipip6.c
+++ b/tunipip6/nss_connmgr_tunipip6.c
@@ -198,6 +198,7 @@ static void nss_tunipip6_encap_exception
 		skb->pkt_type = PACKET_HOST;
 		skb->skb_iif = dev->ifindex;
 		skb->ip_summed = CHECKSUM_NONE;
+		ip_rt_put(rt);
 		netif_receive_skb(skb);
 		return;
 	}
